"/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids runs 75 years, and May to June and October to November each came in under 90% of normal in 36 of them. In 2025 the back end ran short on the middle of the grids, with September to October at 55% and November to December at 48%. The open year has gone the other way so far, with May to June 2026 at 218% on the middle of the grids. Grid 13962 had its driest year in 1954 at 60% of normal.</p>"}
